WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Welcome to the Union Rise Firetruck Training with Supermike, Joël and Steph.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:17.000
We're here today at the firetruck and we're going to learn the best firetruck skills to protect the local region with responsibility, skill and dedication.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.000
The first thing we do today is filling the truck with water.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.000
And where do we fill it?

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.000
At the pump house in the valley.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:50.000
There we have a special connection point to connect the big hose to fill it very quick.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.000
And where does the water come from there?

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.000
From the 1 million litre tank on top of the mountain.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:01.000
And the good news about that is that it's completely electricity free. No pumps, right? It's gravity.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Yeah, there are pumps but it also works without...

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:15.000
So the good news is that if the fire turns away the electric system, may it never happen, we can always have gravity fed water from that tank, right?

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Yes, for sure. And also we have the option to suck water with the pump directly from a river or a spring. So no problem. We always get water.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Right.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:32.000
But for now we train the easy thing to fill it with the water from our own system.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.000
So now we stop the engine again.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:42.000
Maybe you can go or you can see it on the ground where the sun is shining. There is a button.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Yes.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.000
Under the clutch pedal. When you push it then the engine goes off.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Ah, it just shuts it off, yeah?

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.000
And then we make it on the black switch.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.000
Okay.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:01.000
So then everything is off for now. You see? No brakes. This is important. Look here. Lift it. Brake.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.000
Yes.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:07.000
No, we have brakes. Okay, now we go outside and fill the truck.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:17.000
So on the first part here we have all the connections and stuff we need.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:25.000
Also the fire guns. The big one. Only to use with two people, not alone. And the small one.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.000
Now one can be used alone?

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.000
This is the thing we train today.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.000
One person, yeah?

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:38.000
Yes. And then you need the adapter to fill the truck. Follow me.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:49.000
So we have here four connections on this side.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.000
Yes.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:58.000
These are only outlets. So on these places we can connect something to let the water outside from the tank.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:08.000
This on the right side. Easy to see. This is the hose. Not the metal one. It's from rubber. This is the line to fill.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.000
It's the only one, the rubber one.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:16.000
That is the only one to fill. Or when we suck water from a well or a river, then we use this.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.000
That's like a dropper kind of.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:24.000
That is like with a dropper. You can suck without nothing because here we have a pump.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:31.000
And these pumps also can suck the water inside the tank. Not blowing it only out. Also can suck it in.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:34.000
So just so we can. These four are outlets and this is an inlet.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:40.000
This is the only inlet. Later I will mark this all so that it's easier to notice.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:45.000
But when we do it every week and we collect some practice, I think it's easy to use.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:51.000
So important is always when you work with these materials, they must lock in really tight.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.000
Locking in?

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:59.000
Yeah. So now you see it's okay. When it's like this, it's dangerous because we have a lot of pressure and it cannot explode.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.000
Yes.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:09.000
So okay. Now then we take these, these holes always is here because we use these holes for filling.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:19.000
Now we connect this. Then we must make it on a straight way. Like this.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:33.000
Okay. And now next step, open this tap. So now it's open. Now we can go to the point here.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:43.000
Here we have the big wheel with the open and closed sign. When we do it like this, we open.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:49.000
First slowly a little bit to fill the, the holes. And then.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:56.000
And now you can listen. So now we go back to the truck.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:06.000
And you can see here in the middle, there is a transparent hose where we can see the level from the tank.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:12.000
Now you can see here. You see how it moves.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.000
Yep.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:18.000
And so you can see how it fills.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:24.000
So maybe Steph, you can go on the vent here, there.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:31.000
So now we wait, but it goes very quick. So it's not full power now. It's only to show.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:33.000
So full power is even quicker.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:36.000
It's more open. Yeah.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.000
Full power is even quicker, right?

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.000
Yeah, it's much quicker.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.000
So you can do it like in a minute and be going, right?

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:50.000
Yeah, I think it was 120 or something like that. I stopped it one time.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:56.000
It depends also on the pump hose. Now I saw the filters and everything is back flashing.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:03.000
So I think we have not so much pressure like when the system is not in use.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:08.000
But you see it's three and a half thousand liters and it goes very quick.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.000
Now this part is completely full. Now you can see it later here.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:20.000
I think in 10 seconds the level comes up.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:25.000
Always when we don't use the connection points, close them.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.000
Always close, yeah.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:31.000
Like this because you have here rubber rings also here.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:34.000
And when they are in the sun, they get damaged.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:36.000
They get damaged, makes sense.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:39.000
Now you see how it starts shaking?

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.000
Yeah.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.000
That is because of the amount of water coming inside.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:45.000
The tank is getting full and it's shaking.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.000
Now you see now the level.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:48.000
Yep.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.000
Now it goes up.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.000
How many liters is a full tank?

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.000
Three and a half thousand.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.000
So it's a lot.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:57.000
It's a lot.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.000
How much is a Jopper that we have?

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.000
I don't know exactly.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:04.000
Do you know how much it's inside the Jopper?

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.000
Three thousand.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:06.000
Three thousand.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:09.000
Okay, so then we have six and a half thousand liters.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:14.000
So it's also possible to go with both vehicles.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:19.000
First the fire truck and directly behind the truck door.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:22.000
And the Jopper also have an out-touch system.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:26.000
There's a gasolina pump and also we have hoses there.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:36.000
And also the fire gun so we can use both machines separately.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:40.000
Now you can see we are coming up and up and up.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:45.000
Now you see the good thing is from the water the black parts looking different.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:49.000
Like behind because now you can see easy how full it is.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:50.000
Ah yes.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.000
Steph start a little bit closing, not too much.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:07.000
So once it's getting like almost you start closing right?

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.000
Yeah.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:14.000
There is not a problem to overfill because we have a big hole in the roof.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:17.000
And there the water comes out when it's too full.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.000
Okay, so there's no problem.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:23.000
It's nice to see when it goes up that we slowly start going off.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.000
Great.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:28.000
So no potential of catastrophe from overfill.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.000
Yeah.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:30.000
It's good.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:37.000
Is there any down-touch to having the top open?

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.000
Like anything going inside?

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.000
No.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.000
Because this is special, yeah close.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.000
This is special filtered water.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:50.000
It's not prepared with claw or something like the drink water.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.000
But it's filtered water.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:55.000
All the points we have different points here on the land.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:09:02.000
I think they are not all connected because the AgriElectrica didn't do that.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:08.000
But for the future we will go forward to have different points on all the technical walls we have here around.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:15.000
Later we have points where we can connect the hose to suck water for the tank.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:16.000
Yes.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:19.000
One of these big hoses is always inside the truck.

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:24.000
So when we are on the road in the land area we can stop in every place and fill it there.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.000
Yes.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.000
When everything is already installed.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.000
So now we close it again.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:37.000
Then we can remove the connection.

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:39.000
Only the hose put down.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.000
This we put here.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:43.000
Important close again.

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:46.000
Also important because of somebody who's playing.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:52.000
When somebody opens it here or here without engine it's also leaking.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:56.000
Because the tank is full and with 3,500 liters.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:58.000
So this is the closed position right?

00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:59.000
It's opposite to the direction.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:00.000
Yes.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.000
That is always the closed position.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.000
Exactly.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:03.000
When you open and it looks like that.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:04.000
Exactly.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:05.000
Okay.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:06.000
So now we go back in.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.000
Yep.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:11.000
And then we go and empty the truck.